      "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\nMiniCPM pads image slices to the largest patch count in the batch. `VisionAscendAttention` removes those padded rows before FIA, then scatters the compact result into an output allocated with `torch.empty_like(q)`. Only valid rows are written, so padding retains uninitialized memory (or stale graph workspace contents).\r\n\r\nAn Ascend A3 reproduction with MiniCPM-V-2.6 produced slice lengths `[1014, 1036, 1036]`: 3086 valid rows in a 3108-row padded tensor. The first vision attention output had no nonfinite values in valid rows but 49 in padding. Nonfinite values subsequently appeared in the resampler output, and greedy decoding repeated `!` without reaching EOS. Requests without an explicit output limit continued decoding.\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\n- Allocate zero-initialized outputs with `torch.zeros_like(q)` in the eager and metadata paths.\r\n- Clear the existing graph output workspace in place with `output_ws.zero_()` before reuse, preserving the workspace allocation.\r\n- Restore FIA results into the initialized output without additional clearing at writeback.\r\n- Add deterministic regression coverage for valid Q/K/V packing, restored results, and zero padding across eager, metadata, and graph paths, including an unpadded control. Graph tests start with a NaN-filled workspace.\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npython -m pytest test/registered/unit/layers/attention/test_vision_backend_selection.py -q\r\n```\r\n\r\n- Updated PR Python source: **25 passed** on Ascend A3, including all 9 padding regression combinations.\r\n- The same 9 combinations against the original implementation previously produced **6 failed, 3 passed**; all padded combinations fail and the unpadded controls pass.\r\n- Ascend A3 / CANN 9.1.0 B100 runtime (`8dbf2b366b690d83843c42498e972745a89072ee`) with the updated implementation: **1/1 passed** for `TestMiniCPMo26Server.test_image_prefix_cache_reuse` in **123.068 s**, including server startup and cleanup. The test retained `temperature=0`, `max_tokens=32`, and decode graph maximum batch size 4.\r\n- All four image requests produced normal descriptions. The three requests for the same image returned identical text; the logo image returned different text. The repeated `!` assertion failure was absent.\r\n- Verified that the Attention class applied to the B100 runtime matches the updated PR implementation.\r\n\r\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\r\n\r\nNo throughput benchmark. Newly allocated outputs are initialized to zero; graph execution clears the existing workspace. The unpadded path continues returning the FIA output directly.\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] Ruff formatting and lint, isort, and `git diff --check` passed for changed files.\r\n- [x] Added regression tests and verified failure before / success after the fix.\r\n- [x] Reran the MiniCPM-o-2.6 prefix cache case on Ascend A3 with the updated initialization.\r\n- [x] No public API or configuration changes requiring documentation.\r\n\r\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #39219122898](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39219122898)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39219122699](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39219122699)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39219122707](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39219122707)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\r\n",
